<title>USA: TABLE-Travelers Group unit sells notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Travelers Group unit sells notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche debt issue from Commercial Credit Co, a unit of Travelers Group Inc, was priced on Monday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers Inc.</p>
<p>Travelers Group is a diversified financial services company.</p>
<p>BORROWER COMMERCIAL CREDIT COMPANY</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 6.45 PCT   MATURITY 7/1/2002</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.914  FIRST PAY DATE 1/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 6.47 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD 32.4 BPS   CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 6.75 PCT   MATURITY 7/1/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.675  FIRST PAY DATE 1/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 6.795 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD 54 BPS     CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
